{"body":"## Goal\nEstablish Lord Cricket XXVI as a repeatable, tested Codex development project on the recovered `main` branch. This is the **first Codex task**, not an authorisation to start M7K or change the gameplay model.\n\n## Starting evidence\n- Private repo: `SamForbes70/lord-cricket-xxvi`\n- Current migration HEAD at handover: `b8e38e9614fc4340218033b8c42b5a0162e2cf3b`.\n- Historical Pass 22 / M7J source: `5b8b9da990d657197fb56bbfd33152f87b875f5c`.\n- Repo instructions: `AGENTS.md`; full task: `docs/codex-migration/FIRST_CODEX_TASK.md`.\n- Runtime: Node.js >=22.12, npm, Python 3. TypeScript monorepo and browser-based Vite app.\n- Existing alpha is `SYNTHETIC_ALPHA`; M7F-J research only, not production.\n\n## Work requested\n1. Read `AGENTS.md`, `CODEX_START_HERE.md`, `docs/codex-migration/FIRST_CODEX_TASK.md`, `docs/CAPABILITY_MATRIX.md`, `docs/NEXT_PASS.md`, relevant ADRs.\n2. Verify Git ancestry, clean checkout, dependency/toolchain versions, package-lock integrity; do not modify frozen scoring, RNG, generator or match-event contracts.\n3. Run `npm ci`, `npm run schemas:check`, `npm run build`, `npm run typecheck`, `npm run lint`, unit suites, scoring/RNG/probability/generator vectors, management full-season acceptance, and Python M7 tests where data and toolchain permit.\n4. On authorised **local Windows** browser host, install Playwright browsers as needed and execute real Chromium/Firefox tests, IndexedDB save and restore, keyboard/150% UI, season management, and portable career export/import. Cloud-only tests must not be mislabelled Windows/browser acceptance.\n5. Record `PASS / FAIL / BLOCKED / NOT RUN` per gate, exact commands and logs. Do not count inherited historical results as fresh execution.\n6. Create `docs/codex-migration/CODEX_ENVIRONMENT_ACCEPTANCE.md` and recommend one bounded next pass. Fix only evidenced blockers with regression coverage; keep the initial work on a separate branch/PR and do not automatically merge.\n\n## Acceptance\n- Baseline identity checked and historical git ancestry preserved.\n- Environment and test matrix with transparent evidence, including known blockers.\n- No silent data migrations; no fake empirical promotion or exaggerated T20 scoring realism.\n- Clearly documented, reproducible next development task.\n\n## Important\nThe Cricsheet raw JSON archive is not tracked in this repo, and personal IndexedDB saves are not bundled. Both should be handled separately when explicitly available.","state":"OPEN","title":"Codex 00: verify Windows environment and accept recovered Pass 22 baseline","url":"https://github.com/SamForbes70/lord-cricket-xxvi/issues/1"}
